1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,773
This is Form Canvas, a drag-and-drop form designer widget for Mendix.

2
00:00:04,962 --> 00:00:10,911
It draws your own form model, and your app's microflows keep the data, the rules and the versions.

3
00:00:11,212 --> 00:00:12,383
Let's build a form.

4
00:00:13,659 --> 00:00:16,545
Every form has its own place in the forms list.

5
00:00:16,925 --> 00:00:20,202
A new form asks for its settings first. A name,

6
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:25,786
a wizard with steps, or a single page without steps,

7
00:00:26,125 --> 00:00:27,847
how many steps to start with,

8
00:00:28,359 --> 00:00:31,073
and a horizontal or a vertical step bar.

9
00:00:31,458 --> 00:00:36,060
Create and open: the form is ready, with one section for each step.

10
00:00:36,724 --> 00:00:39,524
Drag a field type from the palette into a step.

11
00:00:40,324 --> 00:00:41,776
Add as many as you need.

12
00:00:46,023 --> 00:00:49,448
The width chip makes a field half, or a third of the row.

13
00:00:55,609 --> 00:00:57,735
Now the two fields share one row.

14
00:01:04,142 --> 00:01:07,923
Here is a complete example: a leave request with three steps.

15
00:01:08,355 --> 00:01:14,488
Each field shows chips: what it depends on, what its rules do, its access and its flags.

16
00:01:15,891 --> 00:01:18,556
Click a field to edit it in the docked inspector.

17
00:01:18,964 --> 00:01:24,447
Its label and its help have a box for every language: English, Arabic and Spanish.

18
00:01:24,822 --> 00:01:30,147
The options can come from the field's own list, a shared lookup list, or an external list.

19
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:35,204
Here they follow the unit: each option can belong under one of the unit's values.

20
00:01:35,839 --> 00:01:38,933
And an option like Other can ask the person for details.

21
00:01:40,206 --> 00:01:45,665
Computed fields have a formula: working days are counted between the first and the last day.

22
00:01:46,252 --> 00:01:49,113
Starting values and limits are set the same way.

23
00:01:49,973 --> 00:01:53,937
Rules are typed, never code. This one makes the reason required.

24
00:01:54,304 --> 00:01:58,403
All conditions of a group must hold, and any group is enough.

25
00:01:58,972 --> 00:02:03,475
A condition compares with a value, or with another field, and can be negated.

26
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:10,504
Then: show, hide, require, lock, set a value, or stop the form with a message.

27
00:02:12,872 --> 00:02:17,731
The access view sets every section and field, per workflow stage and role.

28
00:02:18,323 --> 00:02:21,613
Hidden, shown, editable, or required.

29
00:02:21,973 --> 00:02:25,104
And Preview as shows the form the way that stage sees it.

30
00:02:31,288 --> 00:02:34,983
The live preview is the real form, with real inputs.

31
00:02:35,455 --> 00:02:38,022
Fill in the first step, and Next checks it.

32
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:47,572
Choose Unpaid: paid leave disappears, and the reason becomes required.

33
00:02:48,153 --> 00:02:50,524
Choose Other, and the form asks which.

34
00:02:50,717 --> 00:02:53,382
Next will not go on until the step is complete.

35
00:02:59,735 --> 00:03:02,315
One form has a text for every language.

36
00:03:02,752 --> 00:03:06,201
Edit in Arabic, and the canvas turns right to left.

37
00:03:06,649 --> 00:03:11,986
Missing translations show on the canvas, and required languages are checked before publishing.

38
00:03:12,888 --> 00:03:15,504
Check writes each problem on its own field.

39
00:03:18,551 --> 00:03:22,540
Publish creates a new version, and keeps the older ones read-only.

40
00:03:26,683 --> 00:03:30,561
Lookup lists, languages and stages are shared by every form.

41
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:36,183
A value's parent is picked from a list, with a search, so dependent lists cannot break.

42
00:03:36,587 --> 00:03:38,309
And dark mode is built in.

43
00:03:39,168 --> 00:03:42,960
Form Canvas will be available soon on the Mendix Marketplace.

44
00:03:43,563 --> 00:03:46,645
We tried to cover every case a form builder needs.

45
00:03:47,061 --> 00:03:50,608
Try the demo app from the link in the post, and tell us what you think.

